WEBVTT

00:38.430 --> 00:46.770
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

01:57.590 --> 02:03.010
<b>Episode 9 "Father and Daughter Meet New People"</b>

02:00.800 --> 02:04.020
Don't move.
Make a sound and I'll cut you down.

02:05.640 --> 02:07.820
What are you doing here?

02:07.820 --> 02:11.670
I haven't forgiven you for 
what you did in Bordeaux.

02:12.710 --> 02:15.450
So, what? You gonna kill us?

02:16.350 --> 02:19.120
If that's what's best for the world...

02:19.670 --> 02:22.120
Please! Don't kill Byaku!

02:22.350 --> 02:25.120
Silence. I won't show mercy 
just because you're children.

02:25.360 --> 02:27.890
We'll do anything to earn your forgiveness.

02:27.890 --> 02:29.630
Please, just spare his life.

02:30.090 --> 02:34.710
She's returning the money to the 
families who bought her talismans.

02:35.160 --> 02:39.680
Once that's done, we're going 
to Bordeaux to settle matters.

02:40.360 --> 02:42.360
You expect me to believe that?

02:42.360 --> 02:46.670
No, I don't.
 I'm only speaking up for her honor.

02:53.750 --> 02:54.940
I've changed my mind.

02:55.210 --> 02:56.890
I still haven't forgiven you,

02:56.890 --> 02:59.450
but I can't kill a man 
who won't even defend himself.

03:00.370 --> 03:02.660
Th-Thank you so much.

03:04.790 --> 03:07.450
I've got a lot of questions for you.

03:13.970 --> 03:16.490
Jeez, just how many people hate you?

03:16.910 --> 03:18.560
They're with the Inquisition.

03:19.600 --> 03:21.850
Of the Lucrecian Holy Court.

03:32.810 --> 03:35.700
Magic and medicine have robbed 
them of their sense of self.

03:35.700 --> 03:37.330
They'll attack until they're dead.

03:37.330 --> 03:38.660
We have to kill them.

03:39.040 --> 03:40.060
I don't like this.

03:55.730 --> 03:58.860
Killing people really
 doesn't sit right with me...

03:58.860 --> 04:01.590
Come with me. There's much I want to ask.

04:07.420 --> 04:10.180
So, who are the Inquisition?

04:10.180 --> 04:13.330
An underground order 
of the Lucrecian Holy Court

04:13.330 --> 04:17.730
that secretly deals with heretics 
and those who defy the court.

04:18.120 --> 04:20.470
And why are they coming after you?

04:20.760 --> 04:23.520
It all started when my father,

04:23.520 --> 04:27.650
a bishop of Lucrecia, 
got caught up in a power struggle.

04:28.360 --> 04:32.090
He was falsely accused 
and branded a heretic.

04:32.530 --> 04:34.970
So you were acting as a heretical saint

04:34.970 --> 04:37.320
to avenge your murdered parents?

04:38.130 --> 04:39.910
I believed what I was saying.

04:41.490 --> 04:46.320
That's why I was able to do those things...

04:48.380 --> 04:53.090
But I decided to stop it all
 after I lost my ring.

04:53.570 --> 04:56.120
I hate the cult of Vienna,

04:56.120 --> 05:00.250
but I doubt my father or mother 
would approve of seeking revenge.

05:00.620 --> 05:05.120
Yet in spite of that, you raised 
Seren's late father from the grave?

05:10.970 --> 05:15.610
Count Malta was the one who ordered us
 to use the late Count Bordeaux.

05:17.320 --> 05:21.890
If... If only I hadn't done that, then...

05:23.780 --> 05:27.390
<i>What would my dad do 
in a situation like this?</i>

05:28.530 --> 05:31.250
<i>I doubt he'd be so quick to forgive them,</i>

05:31.250 --> 05:34.590
<i>but I don't think he'd be 
too hard on a child, either.</i>

05:42.390 --> 05:44.300
You're pretty badly hurt.

05:44.800 --> 05:49.780
Some people beat me for being a liar
 when I returned their money.

05:49.780 --> 05:52.460
Byaku always comes to my rescue, but still...

05:57.960 --> 06:02.400
I can't leave you unsupervised, 
and I have lots of questions.

06:02.400 --> 06:04.220
You should stay the night here.

06:05.940 --> 06:08.230
We might kill you in your sleep.

06:09.400 --> 06:12.720
You think you can kill me?

06:15.900 --> 06:18.720
Your pretty hair is in shambles.

06:20.200 --> 06:22.290
I'll take you to the baths tomorrow.

06:22.740 --> 06:24.360
What? But...

06:24.360 --> 06:27.850
I haven't forgiven you. 
Just until we reach Bordeaux...

06:28.850 --> 06:29.530
Hey.

06:30.360 --> 06:31.230
What?

06:31.230 --> 06:34.340
You can teleport, right?

06:34.340 --> 06:36.530
That was a borrowed spell.

06:36.820 --> 06:41.120
Now that I've broken away from them,
 I can't cast it anymore.

06:41.120 --> 06:44.230
Seriously? That sure makes you useless.

06:44.230 --> 06:45.510
Well, excuse me.

06:45.970 --> 06:49.950
No matter. I'll protect you 
until we reach Bordeaux.

06:50.390 --> 06:52.340
So you can make proper amends.

06:53.420 --> 06:54.400
I will!

07:02.210 --> 07:04.250
How dare you feign composure!

07:04.250 --> 07:05.910
You'll regret underestimating me!

07:07.730 --> 07:09.450
So she doesn't understand...

07:17.260 --> 07:20.880
Have it your way. I'm game to keep going!

07:21.900 --> 07:23.020
I don't believe it!

07:23.360 --> 07:25.650
What are you two doing here?

07:25.650 --> 07:29.630
The whole night went by, so we thought 
something might've happened.

07:29.630 --> 07:32.320
I see. It's been that long already?

07:32.320 --> 07:36.440
The warped space must affect 
the passage of time, too.

07:36.440 --> 07:38.700
What's going on here?

07:40.240 --> 07:41.490
Lady Marguerite!

07:41.490 --> 07:43.110
We've got to help her!

07:43.110 --> 07:45.800
No, she must learn this for herself.

07:46.580 --> 07:50.650
Don't worry. That thing is not 
strong enough to kill her.

07:51.680 --> 07:54.290
Is the child a demon king?

07:54.290 --> 07:59.040
I must say I don't sense any
 malice or hostility from it.

07:59.040 --> 08:01.670
Marguerite has not realized as much.

08:03.370 --> 08:04.730
I'm scared.

08:09.860 --> 08:11.410
What are you doing here?!

08:11.410 --> 08:13.980
We'll talk later. Lord Graham!

08:15.560 --> 08:17.780
Not yet! I can keep fighting!

08:17.780 --> 08:18.970
Marguerite.

08:19.280 --> 08:20.560
Be reasonable.

08:31.510 --> 08:34.270
We should retreat. 
There's no point in further fighting.

08:34.270 --> 08:35.790
Did you figure something out?

08:36.360 --> 08:39.760
The little guy's just a scared child.

08:39.760 --> 08:43.580
He's only trying to protect himself. 
Nothing more.

08:43.580 --> 08:45.160
Hm, I thought so.

08:45.160 --> 08:46.400
Duncan, we're leaving.

08:46.400 --> 08:47.690
Got it!

08:47.690 --> 08:49.510
I'll bring up the rear.

08:51.360 --> 08:52.850
So lonely...

08:57.670 --> 08:59.570
What a troublesome girl.

09:00.070 --> 09:03.410
I hope she learns her lesson.

09:03.410 --> 09:05.680
I've been there, Lord Graham.

09:05.960 --> 09:09.340
I raised her and taught her to wield a sword.

09:09.830 --> 09:13.300
She's been keen on the outside 
world since she was a child,

09:13.300 --> 09:15.570
always wanting to hear my stories.

09:15.930 --> 09:19.780
We elves care little for
 ourselves as individuals,

09:19.780 --> 09:25.300
and yet it would seem that 
Marguerite seeks personal recognition.

09:26.170 --> 09:30.560
However, elves that leave the 
forest live solitary lives.

09:30.560 --> 09:35.290
Even if they return, it takes time 
for them to be accepted again.

09:35.540 --> 09:38.770
I know this because I experienced it myself.

09:38.770 --> 09:41.800
That's why I keep telling you to
 mind your own business, Granduncle!

09:42.150 --> 09:44.540
You're awake. How are you feeling?

09:44.540 --> 09:48.940
Are you satisfied now that this
 has turned out like you wanted?

09:49.230 --> 09:52.300
Why must you always be so cynical?

09:52.300 --> 09:54.460
Your inconsiderate behavior will—

09:54.460 --> 09:56.230
I've had enough of your lectures!

09:58.340 --> 10:01.820
You mustn't move about! 
Your wounds haven't healed yet!

10:02.830 --> 10:05.350
I bet you had your laughs at my expense, too.

10:05.350 --> 10:09.710
You had a great time watching a reckless idiot
 charge in and get her ass handed to her!

10:09.110 --> 10:10.710
That's enough!

10:10.960 --> 10:15.120
Both Mr. Duncan and Mr. Belgrieve 
were worried about you.

10:15.370 --> 10:18.090
How can anyone give you 
the recognition you crave

10:18.090 --> 10:20.630
when you keep pushing everyone away?

10:24.060 --> 10:25.400
Lady Marguerite!

10:25.400 --> 10:27.390
Let her go, Mr. Duncan.

10:28.110 --> 10:30.400
What a foolish girl.

10:33.220 --> 10:34.650
Mr. Belgrieve?

10:34.930 --> 10:39.780
I have a daughter of my own,
 so I understand how you feel.

10:39.780 --> 10:42.870
You're just as angry at yourself deep down.

10:43.270 --> 10:44.620
But...

10:44.620 --> 10:48.800
Sometimes we dig our heels in 
when it comes to the people we love.

10:48.800 --> 10:51.550
How about leaving this one to me?

10:52.740 --> 10:54.110
I appreciate it.

11:01.370 --> 11:04.310
What do you want? I don't need your pity.

11:04.650 --> 11:09.500
That's not why I'm here. 
I thought we could talk a little.

11:10.250 --> 11:12.320
I have nothing to say to you.

11:12.320 --> 11:14.540
I'm a humble swordsman myself.

11:14.540 --> 11:17.320
I respect your incredible skill with a blade.

11:17.870 --> 11:21.450
I'm only eighteen. 
You don't have to be so polite with me.

11:21.720 --> 11:25.150
Is that so? Then perhaps
 I'll speak a bit more freely.

11:28.710 --> 11:30.830
You taught your daughter to use a sword?

11:30.830 --> 11:32.460
Are you good enough for that?

11:32.750 --> 11:37.910
No. My daughter was just naturally gifted. 
Like you, I'd say.

11:38.350 --> 11:44.480
Even without Lord Graham's instruction,
you would've been a fabulous fighter.

11:44.750 --> 11:47.860
Don't get it twisted. I won't deny my talent,

11:47.860 --> 11:51.510
but I'm only this strong because
 my granduncle was my mentor.

11:51.510 --> 11:56.160
If she'd trained with him, 
your daughter would be even stronger, too.

11:56.460 --> 12:00.900
I see. It sounds like you hold 
Lord Graham in high esteem.

12:03.640 --> 12:07.000
I used to be an adventurer, too.

12:07.660 --> 12:11.430
I had hopes, dreams, and confidence.

12:11.430 --> 12:15.170
I never doubted I'd realize
 my vision of the future,

12:15.170 --> 12:17.950
so I think I know how you feel.

12:18.680 --> 12:21.800
But look at where all that got me.

12:23.770 --> 12:27.310
You loved hearing the tales of 
Graham's travels, didn't you?

12:28.770 --> 12:29.730
Yeah.

12:31.460 --> 12:34.890
Well, let's return to the house. 
You must be hungry.

12:35.260 --> 12:36.120
Yeah.

12:43.180 --> 12:45.010
Um, I...

12:45.010 --> 12:48.330
Mary, I was too harsh. I'm sorry.

12:48.780 --> 12:52.820
Yeah, I... I'm sorry too.

13:07.610 --> 13:09.340
Mother...

13:10.790 --> 13:13.350
There's nothing motherly about me.

13:16.150 --> 13:17.940
G-Good morning!

13:17.940 --> 13:20.960
I-It's just been a long since
 I've slept in a proper bed, so I...

13:20.960 --> 13:22.740
I'm not going to eat you.

13:24.720 --> 13:27.230
Let's get some breakfast. And you!

13:28.260 --> 13:30.240
I'm awake. What do you want?

13:30.510 --> 13:32.910
Give me a hand.
 We'll hit the guild after we eat.

13:34.620 --> 13:39.410
We once got into a fight 
with the local guild master.

13:44.860 --> 13:47.470
Don't worry. I'm here with you.

13:47.470 --> 13:48.420
Okay.

13:51.040 --> 13:52.510
Can I call you Char?

13:52.510 --> 13:54.390
What? Oh, that's fine.

13:54.390 --> 13:57.170
And you can think of me as your big sister.

13:57.170 --> 13:59.560
Um, my big sister?

14:01.290 --> 14:02.920
You can call me that, too.

14:03.440 --> 14:04.850
You can't be serious.

14:06.000 --> 14:07.950
I see...

14:09.070 --> 14:10.190
Good morning, Ange.

14:10.490 --> 14:11.400
Hey.

14:11.400 --> 14:12.690
Who are they?

14:12.690 --> 14:16.250
I, for one, definitely recognize those two...

14:16.250 --> 14:16.700
What?

14:17.190 --> 14:20.200
I'd actually like to talk 
to you about something.

14:23.420 --> 14:24.710
I see.

14:25.060 --> 14:27.310
The Inquisition, huh?

14:27.310 --> 14:31.210
I'd heard rumors, 
but I can't believe they actually exist.

14:31.480 --> 14:34.710
I hope this doesn't get us in 
hot water with the Holy Court.

14:35.070 --> 14:38.720
If that's what's up, it's safest 
for you to stay with Ange.

14:39.120 --> 14:42.590
But I've done lots of bad things.

14:42.590 --> 14:45.780
I'm afraid I can't atone with
 anything short of my life.

14:46.600 --> 14:48.020
Do you want to die?

14:48.650 --> 14:50.020
No.

14:50.290 --> 14:53.290
Then don't casually speak
 of forfeiting your life.

14:53.290 --> 14:56.770
We'll find a way for you to atone later.

14:56.770 --> 15:01.030
So for now, we can't allow a 
mysterious organization to kill you.

15:01.300 --> 15:02.290
Got it?

15:03.090 --> 15:04.130
Yes.

15:04.770 --> 15:07.800
Besides, you don't need
 to worry with me around.

15:08.110 --> 15:10.820
Now that that's settled, 
we're heading to the baths.

15:10.820 --> 15:12.710
You need some new clothes, too.

15:12.710 --> 15:14.700
What? That sounds fun.

15:14.700 --> 15:16.470
Can I come with?

15:16.470 --> 15:18.590
You just want to dress her up like a doll.

15:20.090 --> 15:24.550
You can help, but as her sister, 
I won't allow you to treat her like a toy.

15:24.550 --> 15:26.110
That's not the problem here.

15:24.550 --> 15:26.110
I wouldn't dream of doing that!

15:41.340 --> 15:42.720
You're in a good mood.

15:44.160 --> 15:48.140
I've always wanted to have a 
boisterous time with a crowd.

15:48.450 --> 15:50.710
Elves don't throw parties?

15:50.710 --> 15:55.140
We do, but everyone's so stiff and stuffy.

15:55.530 --> 15:58.640
I bet my granduncle really enjoyed it, too.

15:59.290 --> 16:01.510
Thanks for the invitation, Bel.

16:01.800 --> 16:04.480
We're just glad you could come.

16:05.090 --> 16:06.520
Thanks, Mary.

16:16.970 --> 16:19.290
Welcome back. How'd it go?

16:19.290 --> 16:21.450
Something's not right.

16:21.450 --> 16:23.670
The animals are unsettled.

16:23.670 --> 16:26.310
They're frozen to the 
spot and refuse to move.

16:26.310 --> 16:29.770
It's because the flow of the 
forest's mana has changed.

16:29.770 --> 16:32.300
There must be something afoot.

16:32.610 --> 16:34.060
You think so, too?

16:34.300 --> 16:37.300
In that case, I'll go check it out.

16:37.300 --> 16:38.510
I'll go with you.

16:38.890 --> 16:40.570
In that case, so will I.

16:40.570 --> 16:43.510
Actually, I'd like you to watch the town.

16:43.510 --> 16:46.540
We'll be in trouble if monsters 
show up while we were gone.

16:46.540 --> 16:48.320
Lord Graham isn't feeling well.

16:48.610 --> 16:51.310
I apologize for my foolishness.

16:51.310 --> 16:54.210
You couldn't refuse any drinks
 because you wanted

16:54.210 --> 16:57.560
to dispel the townsfolk's 
prejudices toward elves, right?

16:59.280 --> 17:01.500
I'll defend the village.

17:01.500 --> 17:04.500
I hope you two can figure 
out what's causing this.

17:05.890 --> 17:07.070
Shall we, Mary?

17:07.070 --> 17:08.000
Yeah.

17:12.480 --> 17:15.280
Tch... This mana gives me the creeps.

17:15.280 --> 17:17.330
This is why I can't stand demon kings.

17:17.330 --> 17:19.720
Yeah, this miasma is dreadful.

17:30.590 --> 17:32.150
What happened?

17:35.270 --> 17:40.060
The source of all this is dying, 
but the forest is getting worse.

17:40.060 --> 17:41.830
I don't get it.

17:41.830 --> 17:43.880
We don't know if he's causing it.

17:43.880 --> 17:46.930
Mary, is this child's mana 
similar to a demon king's?

17:47.170 --> 17:49.280
It's not just similar.

17:49.280 --> 17:51.420
That thing <i>is</i> a demon king.

18:02.870 --> 18:04.440
Yuck. What is that?

18:04.670 --> 18:06.510
Looks like an amalgamation of monsters.

18:06.510 --> 18:08.360
Is that even possible?

18:08.360 --> 18:11.260
It happens on rare occasion 
in high-rank dungeons,

18:11.660 --> 18:13.770
but this is my first time seeing it.

18:20.490 --> 18:23.150
I'm scared... I'm scared...

18:24.310 --> 18:27.660
That creepy thing is 
absorbing the kid's mana.

18:27.660 --> 18:29.370
It must be the problem!

18:30.180 --> 18:31.290
Look alive.

18:31.290 --> 18:32.850
It must have a core somewhere.

18:32.850 --> 18:35.130
A core? What's it look like?

18:35.130 --> 18:36.790
I don't know,

18:36.790 --> 18:39.790
but its body should be formed around it.

18:39.790 --> 18:42.170
Trace the regeneration back to the core.

18:42.170 --> 18:46.020
I see. Then I'll find it with a swift attack!

18:56.900 --> 18:58.230
Don't die on me.

19:05.010 --> 19:06.690
There it is!

19:17.840 --> 19:20.000
Who lets their guard down 
on the battlefield?!

19:27.760 --> 19:31.130
You got this wound protecting me...

19:31.130 --> 19:33.780
Don't worry about it. It's not serious.

19:34.540 --> 19:38.820
How can I fight like my granduncle?

19:39.090 --> 19:45.570
Well, a moment's decision can spell 
life or death for an adventurer.

19:45.570 --> 19:48.240
So you must never lose your cool.

19:48.240 --> 19:52.540
Always keep a second version of yourself 
behind you to observe your every move.

19:53.130 --> 19:55.590
I take great care to do that.

20:03.970 --> 20:06.490
It's still alive? I'll kill it this time!

20:06.490 --> 20:07.490
There's no end to it.

20:07.490 --> 20:09.410
We have the kid with us. We should flee.

20:09.410 --> 20:10.510
But...

20:19.410 --> 20:21.390
<i>Can we evade it to the bitter end?</i>

20:21.390 --> 20:24.360
<i>No, I'll defend our rear until we can escape!</i>

20:27.890 --> 20:29.360
Granduncle...

20:29.750 --> 20:32.820
Well done, Mary. A commendable effort.

20:32.820 --> 20:34.880
Bel, I'm sorry for the trouble.

20:35.150 --> 20:36.660
How are you feeling?

20:39.970 --> 20:41.440
Not bad.

20:49.640 --> 20:53.590
I've gotten old. One swing, 
and I'm out of breath.

20:54.890 --> 20:56.670
And yet you're still exceptional.

20:56.670 --> 20:59.770
You completely cleared that dreadful miasma.

20:59.770 --> 21:01.610
Thank you, Lord Graham.

21:11.480 --> 21:14.580
Now, now. That's not food.

21:14.580 --> 21:15.990
Who's the kid?

21:16.290 --> 21:19.830
His body is almost completely human,

21:19.830 --> 21:23.520
but the mana within him closely 
resembles a demon king's.

21:23.520 --> 21:28.020
He doesn't have much 
at the moment, though.

21:28.440 --> 21:33.160
Sounds like the situation 
isn't very dire after all.

21:33.160 --> 21:34.010
Indeed.

21:34.290 --> 21:36.530
So, what are we going to do with him?

21:36.890 --> 21:41.520
We can't throw him out now. I'll raise him.

21:42.090 --> 21:43.510
But he's a demon king!

21:44.030 --> 21:47.030
I don't think he's dangerous.

21:49.140 --> 21:54.120
Well, this is your home.
The decision is yours to make.

21:54.120 --> 21:55.530
Thanks, I appreciate it.

21:56.140 --> 21:59.880
That just leaves what Ange will think...

21:59.880 --> 22:02.050
But it is what it is.

23:35.140 --> 23:40.090
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.140 --> 23:40.090
<b>"Wriggling Malice"</b>
